# Styling Guide: Flight Deck

This project uses [Tailwind CSS v4](https://tailwindcss.com) (via `@tailwindcss/vite`). All tokens and design primitives live in [app.css](mdc:src/app.css). Style with utilities in markup; avoid `<style>` blocks.

The look: a flight deck HUD. Flat, square-cornered surfaces, thin corner brackets instead of boxes, mono uppercase captions, and four "livery" stripes as the only accent colours. Day mode is an icy, overexposed field; Night mode is deep space with stars.

## Colour tokens

Each token is `light-dark(<day>, <night>)`; the theme switch only sets `color-scheme` on `<html>` (no attribute = Auto/OS).

| Utility suffix                    | Meaning                                                         |
| --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `canvas`                          | page background                                                 |
| `surface`                         | raised fills: hover states, code blocks, inputs                 |
| `ink`, `ink-2`, `ink-3`           | primary / secondary / meta text                                 |
| `line`, `line-2`                  | hairlines and dividers / stronger outlines and HUD brackets      |
| `link`                            | links and hover highlights                                      |
| `livery-1` … `livery-4`           | the stripes: red-orange, amber, gold, teal. Accents only        |
| `on-livery`                       | text placed on a livery fill                                    |
| `sat`, `planet-a`, `planet-b`     | orbit illustration                                              |

Section colours: Blog `livery-1`, About `livery-2`, Art `livery-4` (see `sections` in `$lib/config`). Tag colours come from `src/lib/content/tags.json`, shared with the OG generator.

`dark:` targets Night, whether chosen explicitly or via Auto on a dark OS.

## Primitives (app.css)

| Utility    | What                                                                                  |
| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `hud`      | corner brackets; recolour with `[--hud-c:…]`                                          |
| `chevron`  | slanted leading edge (buttons, tags, nav flags); cut width via `[--cut:…]`            |
| `livery`   | the four stripes as a background                                                      |
| `eyebrow`  | mono 11.5px uppercase caption in `ink-3`                                              |
| `shadow-frame` | soft drop shadow for images                                                       |

Fonts: `font-display` (Saira, use with `font-stretch-[108%…115%]`) for headings and UI labels, `font-sans` (IBM Plex Sans) for text, `font-mono` (IBM Plex Mono) for meta.

## Rules

- No border radius, except avatars and app icons.
- Containers are marked with `hud` brackets or a single `border-line` hairline, never both.
- Hover = `bg-surface` + bracket colour change, or `text-link`. Arrow links nudge `translate-x`.
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Pause long-running motion off-screen; everything stops under `prefers-reduced-motion` (handled globally).
- Breakpoints follow the layouts: `xs` 520, `sm` 640, `md` 768, `lg` 900, `xl` 1024, `2xl` 1440 (post index sidebar).

## Components

Before writing markup, reuse what exists in `$lib/components`:

- `ui/` primitives: `Button` (primary | ghost), `Tag`, `Chip`, `HudBox`, `Frame` (framed 3:2 or natural-ratio box), `Figure` (`Root`/`Media`/`Corner`/`Caption`: framed media with corner overlays and a caption), `Picture` (enhanced image with blurred placeholder; `sizes` required), `AiFlag`, `PageHeader`, `SectionHeading`, `TechList`, `PillLinks`.
- `layout/`: `Container` (page column), `SiteHeader`, `SiteFooter`, `ThemeSwitch`, `Starfield`, `ReadingProgress`.
- `posts/`: `PostImage` (inline post image by public URL; `ai` flags it as AI-generated), `PostRef` (inline card for another note, placed after the paragraph that first links to it; `hash` deep-links a heading), `PostCard`, `PostRow(s)`, `PostFeature`, `PostMeta`, `PostsByYear`, `SeriesCard`, `SeriesParts`, `PostPager`, `PostIndex` (all-notes rail beside a post, `2xl` and up).
- `home/`, `about/`, `art/`: page sections composed from the above.

## Note links

Every link to a note is built from `posts/note-link`: `NoteLink` (the `<a>`: hover group, zoom area, accent; `boxed` adds brackets), `NoteThumb` (hero image, `framed` for big cards), `NoteTitle` (`lg` featured, `md` cards/rows, `sm` pager/series parts), `NoteArrow` (the arrow; `label` for "Read the note →"-style calls to action). Layouts: `PostFeature` (home), `PostCard` (blog grid), `SeriesCard` / `SeriesParts`, `PostRow` (lists; `boxed` for `PostRef` inline cards and `PostPager`).

- Hover is the same everywhere: title turns `text-link`, image zooms 1.02, arrow nudges. Boxed links also get `bg-surface` and brackets in the accent.
- Accent is always Blog `livery-1`. No hairline-bordered link boxes.
- One arrow per link, always `NoteArrow`. Rows and boxed links put it in a trailing column; cards without one (blog grid, series parts) put it inline after the title's last word, joined with `&nbsp;`.`PostMeta` (tag + date) is the meta line; eyebrows are only for context ("Linked note · 009", "Previous", "Series · 3 parts").

Content (bio, career, projects, art collections, tag labels) lives in `$lib/content`, not in pages.
Images: use `Picture` (or `<enhanced:img>`) via `getPostHeroImage()` / `getArtImage()` / `getPostImage()` and pass a realistic `sizes`.
